	(text "Notes: \n1) The drive is 2-phase-on with no disable, so holding current flows continuously: \n   about 0.84A with 13Ω windings.\n2) R93 dissipates about 4W in normal operation, so its discoloration is expected. \n   CR20 carries the holding current while idle; Q22 raises the common to 24V during \n   steps.\n3) The flyback clamp is about 58V against the TIP110's 60V rating. Use TIP111 or \n   TIP112 as replacements."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
